  "_comment": "Cross-language contract for the charge/discharge power-limit conversion (issue #346). Checked by Rust (src-tauri/src/inverter/power_limit.rs) and TypeScript (tests/lib/powerLimit.test.ts) so the two implementations cannot drift. Generated by an independent third implementation (round half up; HR 111/112 is a percentage of battery capacity, 50 = 0.5C, per GivTCP write.py/read.py; 100% writes 50; a non-zero percentage never writes 0; a capacity outside 1-150 kWh is treated as unknown). bank: half = HR 111/112 (0-50), direct = HR 313/314 and HR 1110/1108 (1-100). Vectors at a rounding tie are omitted so the f32/f64 difference between the two languages cannot matter.",
